WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.730
Harley Quinn is practically the antiheroic
queen of the DC Universe, but the one place

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.550
you aren't going to find her is Zack Snyder's
Justice League.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.099
Even at four hours in length, the film apparently
didn't have room for Margot Robbie's Harley

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.099
amongst the story of the greatest heroes on
Earth battling Steppenwolf from remaking Earth

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:16.129
in Apokolips' image.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:19.990
The outcome of the Justice League Snyder Cut
is similar to that of the theatrical version

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.619
that was released in 2017.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:26.009
However, it's a lot clearer in the director's
cut that Darkseid is coming, and we're left

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:30.359
with one final scene in which Batman and his
crew of misfits wander around the post-apocalyptic

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:32.360
hellscape Batman has a vision of.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.440
It's here, in the premonition of the Knightmare
reality, where Batman has a brief conversation

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.600
with the Joker.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.620
However, Joker's presence in the Snyder Cut
does lead to some questions — the most immediately

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.860
pressing of which regards Harley Quinn.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.570
If Joker's around, then where's his beloved
partner in crime?

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:51.760
In a key piece of dialogue in Zack Snyder's
Justice League, Harley's fate is revealed.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.700
"Isn't that right, Batman?"

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.350
In the film, Batman has another vision of
the Knightmare reality that seems to be what's

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.730
destined to happen when Darkseid comes to
Earth.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:06.891
This sequence shows Batman agreeing to a truce
with the Clown Prince of Crime; however, while

00:01:06.891 --> 00:01:10.130
they don't go at each other's throats in the
moment, it's clear there's still a lot of

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.150
animosity between the two, especially when
Joker brings up the Dark Knight's greatest

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.850
failing: allowing his sidekick Robin to die.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.340
Batman throws this statement back at his arch-nemesis
by mentioning how Harley Quinn died in his

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.340
arms.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.990
He also tells Joker that Harley made him promise
that when he finally killed her ex-boyfriend,

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.040
he had to do it slowly.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.040
Batman tells Joker,

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.780
"She begged me, with her last breath, that
when I killed you — and make no mistake,

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.040
I will f---ing kill you — I do it slow.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.049
And I'm gonna honor that promise."

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:40.020
It's an intense moment, and the magnitude
isn't lost on Joker, who quivers after the

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.020
threat.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.799
No more information is given outside of that,
such as what caused Harley Quinn to die, but

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:49.369
one thing is abundantly clear: She and Joker
definitely probably didn't make up before

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:50.369
her death.

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:54.500
While it seems unlikely at this point that
Justice League 2 will come to fruition, especially

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.619
with Snyder at the helm, we at least know
that Harley probably won't have a role within

00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:00.979
the Knightmare timeline if the project does
happen someday.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:04.110
"That wasn't me."

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.950
So, is there a chance we could actually see
this heartbreaking death scene come up in

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:11.150
a future DCEU film that isn't a Justice League
sequel?

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:12.380
Don't hold your breath.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:16.310
Outside of a role in the upcoming Flash movie,
it's looking more and more unlikely that Affleck

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:19.910
will be the mainline Dark Knight going forward
— especially given the fact that Batman's

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:24.140
getting a solo movie that stars Robert Pattinson
as a younger Bruce Wayne and doesn't seem

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.290
to have anything to do with Snyder's films.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.860
Despite all of the shaky continuity within
the DCEU, Robbie's Harley Quinn appears as

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.760
though she'll continue to be a force in the
franchise going ahead.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.350
In just a few months, she'll appear in The
Suicide Squad, which debuts in theaters and

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.290
on HBO Max on August 6, 2021.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:44.220
Beyond that upcoming movie, it's unclear what
Harley Quinn's cinematic future could entail.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.560
The Suicide Squad writer-director James Gunn
teased on Instagram a while back that he and

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.450
Robbie discussed working together in the future.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:54.780
One would assume if The Suicide Squad is well-received,
a follow-up would be in the cards, with Robbie

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.250
returning to the cast.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.250
There's also the possibility of a sequel to
Birds of Prey as well as a solo Harley Quinn

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.250
movie.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.390
There's a lot of room for growth with the
antiheroine, and DC probably isn't going to

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.950
kill her off any time soon just to make good
on a scene that exists only in a director's

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.850
cut version of a film.

